# builtin-is-contractive
--- uses: ["core"]
# returns true for a TypeNode.Recursive variant.
# The Recursive constructor itself IS guarding (guarding: true in the TypeNode ADT).
# This means an inner μb.T shields any outer recursive variable from RecursiveRef
# nodes inside T — nested recursive types are contractive at the outer binder level.
#
# This covers the case where a type uses another mu-bound type as a child:
#   μa.{head: μb.{val: Int, rest: b}, tail: a}
# At the outer μa level, the body's `head` field is a TypeNode.Recursive — which is
# guarding. So the outer type is contractive.
#
# The Recursive constructor is built manually with builtin-variant since TypeNode
# constructors are only accessible in the type-stage evaluator, not at runtime.
[rec-node:   [builtin-variant "TypeNode.Recursive" [var: "b"  body: 42]]]
[result:     [builtin-is-contractive rec-node]]
=== out
Dict({"result": Bool(true)})
